target/
build/
*.o
*.so
.cache/
compile_commands.json

# Never commit Roblox APKs or anything extracted from them.
*.apk
/apk/
/native/lib/
.flatpak-builder/
*.flatpak

# Per-run engine debris. Roblox writes its FastLog and a per-PID memory-profile
# dump next to the working directory on every launch; some were committed before
# this rule existed, which is why the paths already have contents.
appData/logs/
appData/LocalStorage/_memProfStorage*.json

# Agent worktrees; these are live checkouts, not project content.
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-environment build outputs (just build distrobox|nix)
target-distrobox/
target-nix/
# Any out-of-tree build directory, not a hand-maintained list of the ones that
# exist today. `just build toolbox` makes `target-toolbox/`, agents working in
# parallel make their own to dodge the shared `target/` lock, and three of them
# were swept into a commit by a `git add -A` because the list did not cover them.
target-*/

# The Sober issue corpus (tools/sober-corpus/). Other people's GitHub bug
# reports with no license grant to us — see ADR-017. PII-redacted before it
# ever lands here, but it stays local regardless.
tools/sober-corpus/data/

# The Discord bridge's configuration and credentials. Written 0600 by
# `deno task setup` and `create_github_app.ts`, and holding a bot token, a
# GitHub App private key and a webhook secret in plaintext. These must never be
# committed, and the ignores are here rather than in a nested .gitignore so
# they cannot be removed by deleting that directory's own file.
#
# **The .pem and the .env beside it were untracked and unignored for an hour**
# after the App was created, which `git add -A` would have committed. The
# patterns below are deliberately broader than the three exact names, because
# the next credential this directory acquires will not be called any of them.
tools/discord-bridge/.env
tools/discord-bridge/*.pem
tools/discord-bridge/*.key
tools/discord-bridge/*-app.env
tools/discord-bridge/.env.*
tools/discord-bridge/node_modules/
